From 9eec9a013bcdc423c5a130b3a1748118b07a46bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:09:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Judge the flow governor's gain by its own cuts

Only the bytes pi and the cut at a long queue take count as a cut, once what is in flight has come down with them; a loss, the caps following the round trip and a dip of other traffic's queue no longer read as one. A download that returns no credit in a round stays in the caps for a second, and a queue that halves gives the cuts their gain back.
